        extract_catalog_field(uint16_t, ce_namlen, 0);
        extract_catalog_field(uint16_t, ce_num, 4);
        extract_catalog_field(uint64_t, ce_timestamp, 8);
        reclen = cep->ce_namlen;
        ...
        np = CAST(const uint16_t *, CAST(const void *, (b + 16)));
        nb = CAST(const char *, CAST(const void *, (np + cep->ce_namlen)));
        if (nb > eb) {
                cep->ce_namlen = 0;
                break;
        }
        for (k = 0; k < cep->ce_namlen; k++)
                cep->ce_name[k] = np[k];
```

The `extract_catalog_field` macro checks `if (b + l + sizeof(cep->f) > eb)`. So it reads `ce_namlen` (2 bytes at offset 0), `ce_num` (2 bytes at offset 4), `ce_timestamp` (8 bytes at offset 8). These are checked.

Then `np = b + 16`, and `nb = np + ce_namlen`. If `nb > eb`, break. Then reads `np[k]` for k in [0, ce_namlen). Since `nb = np + ce_namlen` and `nb <= eb`, the reads are within bounds.

